stem_md:
Let the polynomial  $P(x) = x^2 - 2025x + 2025$ . Find all real numbers  $x$  that satisfy the following conditions simultaneously:
\[
\left\{
    \begin{array}{ll}
        P(P(P(x))) = x,

        P(P(x)) + P(x) + x \in \mathbb{Q}
    \end{array}
\right.
\]

Viorel's class children were paired (each boy is paired with a girl) and went to the orchard at Viorel's grandfather to pick apples; it is known that for each pair the boy picked either twice as many apples or half as many apples as the girl, and each child picked at most  $100$  apples; 
(a) If a total of  $2025$  apples were picked, what is the minimum number of children in Viorel's class? 
(b) Could the children have picked  $2026$  apples?

